# CoinScopeAI — Claude Code One-Time Installer
# Updated: 2026-05-19 | Claude Code v2.1.144+
# Run OUTSIDE any venv. Requires: macOS, Node.js 18+, bash.
# After install, launch from the engine repo (see Claude_Code_Agent).

# Step 1: Install Claude Code globally
npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code

# Step 2: Verify version (must be v2.1.144 or later)
claude --version

# Step 3: Login (fresh OAuth handshake)
claude login
# Browser will open → complete login → "Login successful. Press Enter to continue"

# Step 4: Grant macOS folder access
# System Settings → Privacy & Security → Files and Folders
# Enable Claude (or Claude Code) access to:
#   ~/Code folder
#   ~/Documents/Claude folder
# Then relaunch Terminal.

# Step 5: Confirm repos are at correct paths
# v1 engine repo:    ~/Code/CoinScopeAI
# v2 docs repo:      ~/Documents/Claude/Projects/CoinScopeAI_v2
# Mac Cowork root:   ~/Documents/Claude/Projects/CoinScopeAI

# Troubleshooting
# OAuthError 500 / Unable to start session:
#   1. npm update -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
#   2. rm -rf ~/.claude/cache
#   3. claude logout && claude login
#   4. claude doctor   (if still failing)
#   5. Disable VPN before running claude login
#
# "Folder access denied" in Claude Code desktop app:
#   System Settings → Privacy & Security → Files and Folders → enable Claude
#
# zsh: parse error near '\n':
#   Never paste multi-line blocks. Copy and run ONE LINE AT A TIME.
